1) Equivalent to i -= n; return i;.
2) Let D be difference_type:
  * If W is an integer-like type:
       * If W is signed-integer-like, returns D(D(x.value_ ﻿) - D(y.value_ ﻿)).
       * Otherwise, returns y.value_  > x.value_  ? D(-D(y.value_  - x.value_ ﻿)) :
         D(x.value_  - y.value_ ﻿).
  * Otherwise, returns x.value_  - y.value_.

These functions are not visible to ordinary unqualified or qualified lookup, and can only
be found by argument-dependent lookup when iterator is an associated class of the
arguments.

